irst elected in 2024, has out-raised Democrat William Lawrence by roughly five to one and holds a large cash advantage, but Democratic outside groups have spent heavily against him. Lawrence, a climate-focused challenger, has drawn substantial media attention and endorsements in the final weeks.\n\nExpert raters are split: several call it a Tossup while others rate it Lean or Likely Democratic for a flip, and prediction markets put Lawrence's win chances in the mid-to-high 50s. The available polling, all from Democratic-leaning sponsors, shows a narrow two-point race, though the data is sparse and somewhat dated. The race sits as a modest Democratic lean with wide uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6879, "margin": 2.86}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6475, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7011, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6783, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6189, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6168, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6888, "margin": 3.0}]}